note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note gpu/nvidia/driver/nvrm.om: decisions of CUDApp nvrm/nvrm.c (84b524ca) that were still C: which channel a
note put or retire names, the checks before a copy, before an allocation and on the framebuffer heap answer.
note The ioctl, the mapping and the byte copy that follow each check stay with the device shell.

note nvrm_chan_put and nvrm_chan_retire: 0 when ch is the main channel (0), 1 when it is extra channel ch
note (1 to nextra; the table entry is ch - 1), 2 when it names no channel: nvrm_chan_put then answers 0 and
note nvrm_chan_retire does nothing. On 1, nvrm_chan_retire moves the entry's retired count with drv_retire.
fn drv_chan ch ulong nextra ulong to ulong
if eq ch 0
ret 0
end
if le ch nextra
ret 1
end
ret 2
end

note copy_live span: bytes [off, off + bytes) is non-empty and inside an allocation of size bytes
fn drv_span off ulong bytes ulong size ulong to bool
if eq bytes 0
ret false
end
if gt off size
ret false
end
ret le bytes sub size off
end

note copy_live row: live row a (handle, va, size, cpu, cpu_live, rm_live, quarantined) is the allocation m
note (handle, va, size, cpu) with its CPU and RM mappings live and not quarantined
fn drv_lrow a view ulong 7 m view ulong 4 to bool
for i ulong 4
if ne get a i get m i
ret false
end
end
if or eq get a 4 0 eq get a 5 0
ret false
end
ret eq get a 6 0
end

note nvrm_copy_to and nvrm_copy_from before the byte copy: 0 copy; 1 refuse without a message (no caller
note buffer, the client faulted, or the span is empty or outside the allocation); 2 refuse with the message
note "copy requires a live allocation and an in-bounds span" (no live row is the allocation, see drv_lrow)
fn drv_copy buf bool faulted bool off ulong bytes ulong size ulong live bool to ulong
if or not buf faulted
ret 1
end
if not drv_span off bytes size
ret 1
end
if not live
ret 2
end
ret 0
end

note nvrm_alloc_vram: local framebuffer memory is asked for only on a discrete SM86 board
fn drv_vramok discrete bool sm ulong to bool
ret and discrete eq sm 86
end

note alloc_with_cacheability size check: 0 refuses ("invalid or overflowed allocation size": the client
note faulted, size is 0, or rounding it up to 4 KiB passes 2^64 - 1); otherwise the size rounded up to 4 KiB.
note WolframLanguageEvaluator: 2^64 - 1 - 4095 -> 18446744073709547520; BitAnd[BitNot[4095], 2^64-1] -> 18446744073709547520.
fn drv_asize faulted bool size ulong to ulong
if or faulted eq size 0
ret 0
end
if gt size 18446744073709547520
ret 0
end
ret and add size 4095 18446744073709547520
end

note alloc_with_cacheability: the live allocation table of cap rows holding count rows is full
fn drv_livefull count ulong cap ulong to bool
ret ge count cap
end

note nvrm_vram_info on the VID_HEAP_INFO answer: 0 the heap numbers stand; 1 "VID_HEAP_INFO errno" (the
note ioctl failed or RM returned a status); 2 "invalid framebuffer heap information" (total 0 or more free
note than total); 3 refused before the ioctl without a message (not a discrete board)
fn drv_vinfo discrete bool iorc ulong status ulong total ulong avail ulong to ulong
if not discrete
ret 3
end
if or ne iorc 0 ne status 0
ret 1
end
if or eq total 0 gt avail total
ret 2
end
ret 0
end
